### Why It Looks Like It Works Perfectly When You Test It
There are four architectural reasons why broken backend connections stay invisible during normal testing:
1. **Everything writes to `localStorage` and React state first** ([App.tsx](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/App.tsx#L708-L864)), so your browser immediately displays every edit even if the database rejected or ignored it.
2. **`pushServerCatalogPatch` never checks `res.ok` and has an empty `catch {}`** ([App.tsx](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/App.tsx#L289-L332)), and [`applyCatalogPatch`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L1419-L1432) catches D1 SQL errors while still returning HTTP `200` and updating in-memory cache + R2.
3. **Cloudflare Worker isolate cache masks D1 failures for 30+ seconds** ([catalog.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L53-L56)): deleting a promo code or adding an admin looks persisted while hitting the same warm Worker isolate, then silently reverts once a cold isolate reads D1 SQL.
4. **AI Studio runs `server.ts` (Express), while `samoweave.com` runs `functions/` (Cloudflare Pages Functions)** — several endpoints behave differently or only exist in `server.ts` (such as the AI Product Copy Drafter).

