## 3. Critical Security & Data-Loss Findings (Fix Immediately)

### 3.1 Zero Authentication on All Live Cloudflare APIs
Admin login ([AdminDashboard.tsx](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx#L1027-L1028), [App.tsx](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/App.tsx#L3515-L3522)) is **UI-only**. No Firebase ID token is ever sent to or verified by any Cloudflare Function, and every function sets `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. Any anonymous user on the internet can currently:
- **Overwrite your entire store** via `POST /api/catalog` ([catalog.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L1516-L1542)): change prices, wipe products, inject fake promo codes, or alter email/shipping settings.
- **Delete every product photo and hero banner** via `POST /api/r2-delete` ([r2-delete.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/r2-delete.ts#L23-L74)) by passing `{"keys": ["products/...", "banners/..."]}`.
- **Overwrite existing images or upload Stored XSS** via `POST /api/r2-upload` ([r2-upload.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/r2-upload.ts#L33-L193)): accepts caller-supplied `fileName` without a unique prefix (overwriting live product photos) and accepts `contentType: "image/svg+xml"` (stored XSS on `images.samoweave.com`).
- **Send phishing/spam from `orders@samoweave.com`** via `POST /api/order-confirmation-email` ([order-confirmation-email.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/order-confirmation-email.ts#L684-L897)): trusts caller-supplied `customerEmail`, `senderAddress`, `bccAddress` (can be cleared to `""` to hide abuse), and unvalidated `bannerLinkUrl`, using your live `RESEND_API_KEY`.
- **Overwrite your Google Sheet & catalog stock** via `POST /api/sheets-sync` ([sheets-sync.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/sheets-sync.ts#L211-L455)): only `inbound_sheet_edit` checks `GOOGLE_SHEETS_SYNC_SECRET`; both `push_to_sheet` and `pull_from_sheet` have **zero auth** and accept attacker-supplied `payload.products` (which `pull_from_sheet` writes back to D1!).
- **Read or delete all newsletter subscribers** via `GET`/`DELETE /api/newsletter/subscribers` ([subscribers/[[id]].ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/newsletter/subscribers/%5B%5Bid%5D%5D.ts#L23-L126)).

### 3.2 Public Exposure of Customer Orders, Addresses, Emails & Phones
1. **`GET /api/catalog`** ([catalog.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L459-L497), [L1171-L1205](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L1171-L1205)) returns the entire store snapshot to every visitor every 20 seconds, including **`orders`** (customer full names, emails, phone numbers, home shipping addresses), **`newsletterSubscribers`** (emails & phone numbers), **`preorders`**, **`admins`**, **`promoCodes`**, **`hiddenFromStore` products**, and **`adminNotificationState`**. (`sanitizeCatalogStateForClient` only strips Google Sheets credentials.)
2. **Public R2 Backup (`state/catalog.json`)**: [`applyCatalogPatch`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L49) writes the entire `nextState` (including all customer orders and PII) to `state/catalog.json` inside `SAMO_R2_BUCKET`—the exact same public bucket serving `https://images.samoweave.com`. Anyone visiting `https://images.samoweave.com/state/catalog.json` may download the full snapshot directly.
3. **Newsletter Subscribe Leaks All Subscribers**: [`POST /api/newsletter/subscribe`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/newsletter/subscribe.ts#L88-L107) returns `subscribers: allSubscribers` in the JSON response to every anonymous user who subscribes.

### 3.3 Revoked Admin Still Allowed in Firestore Rules
- [`sanitizeAuthorizedAdmins`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/App.tsx#L224-L240) explicitly strips `charbelkorab11123@gmail.com`.
- However, [`firestore.rules`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/firestore.rules#L30-L38) **still hardcodes `charbelkorab11123@gmail.com` inside `isAdmin()`**, giving that account full read/write/delete access to Firestore (including `settings/store_config`).
- Also, [`firebase.json`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/firebase.json#L2-L4) does not specify the named database (`ai-studio-516f891a-8996-49dc-99d8-9ac87a51fe3d` from [firebase-applet-config.json](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/firebase-applet-config.json#L6)), so deploying rules without targeting that DB updates `(default)` instead.

### 3.4 Transient Backend Error Can Overwrite Your Live Catalog With Seed Data
- When `GET /api/catalog` catches any error, it returns **HTTP `200`** with `{ updatedAt: 0, error: "..." }` ([catalog.ts](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/functions/api/catalog.ts#L1239-L1249)).
- On the storefront, [`pullServerCatalog`](file:///home/antigravity/Charr111/samo-store2/src/App.tsx#L1411-L1451) sees `res.ok === true` and `!data.updatedAt`, assumes the database has never been seeded, and **immediately POSTs the visitor's `localStorage` / `INITIAL_PRODUCTS` seed state to `POST /api/catalog`**, risking overwriting your real ~100-item catalog.

